<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marquesas Islands</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Marquesas Islands are a group of rugged volcanic islands in the north-east of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polynesia">Polynesia</a>, among the earliest settled in eastern Polynesia and a likely source of settlers for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hawaii">Hawaii</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-island">Rapa Nui</a>. Visited by the Spanish navigator Álvaro de Mendaña in 1595, they were annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1842. Disease drastically reduced their population in the 19th century; the painter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paul-gauguin">Paul Gauguin</a> died on Hiva Oa in 1903.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marquesas-islands.jpg" alt="Marquesas Islands" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Background: Association MOTU HAKA Tiki's head: Association PATUTIKI Vectorization: Sémhur · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Marquesas_Islands.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
